package api

// sswCurriculumFoodServiceEnglish contains reviewed exact-source translations
// for Food Service curriculum learning materials.
var sswCurriculumFoodServiceEnglish = map[examSSWEnglishKey]string{
	{field: "ssw.description", source: `Menerapkan kebersihan diri, pemisahan bahan, serta kendali waktu dan suhu sesuai rencana kerja restoran. Status program per 22 Oktober 2026: halaman resmi pemerintah menandai penerimaan baru SSW(i) bidang Food Service tidak tersedia; OTAFF juga menghentikan pemesanan ujian SSW(i). Materi belajar tetap dapat dipelajari dan status perlu dicek kembali pada sumber resmi.`}: `Apply personal hygiene, ingredient separation, and time and temperature controls according to the restaurant's work plan. Program status as of October 22, 2026: the official government page indicates that new SSW(i) applications in Food Service are unavailable; OTAFF has also stopped accepting SSW(i) exam bookings. The learning materials remain available, and the status should be checked again against official sources.`,
	{field: "ssw.title", source: `Kondisi tubuh dan persiapan sebelum giliran`}:                                                                     `Health and Preparation Before a Shift`,
	{field: "ssw.objective", source: `Melaporkan gejala sakit dan menyiapkan seragam, rambut, kuku, serta perlengkapan sebelum menangani makanan.`}: `Report illness symptoms and prepare your uniform, hair, nails, and equipment before handling food.`,
	{field: "ssw.objective", source: `Memilih tindakan aman pada satu situasi kerja dan menjelaskan alasannya.`}:                                    `Choose a safe action in a work situation and explain why.`,
	{field: "ssw.objective", source: `Menggunakan ungkapan Jepang sederhana untuk meminta konfirmasi atau melaporkan keadaan.`}:                     `Use simple Japanese expressions to ask for confirmation or report a situation.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Pekerja restoran menyentuh bahan, alat, piring, dan permukaan yang digunakan pelanggan. Gejala seperti demam, diare, atau muntah serta luka pada tangan dapat meningkatkan risiko cemaran. Setiap tempat memiliki aturan pelaporan dan penugasan; pekerja memberi tahu pemimpin agar tugas aman ditentukan sebelum mulai.`}: `Restaurant workers handle ingredients, tools, dishes, and surfaces used by customers. Symptoms such as fever, diarrhea, or vomiting, as well as hand injuries, can increase contamination risks. Each workplace has reporting and task-assignment rules; tell the supervisor so safe duties can be assigned before work begins.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Sebelum giliran, ganti seragam, tutup rambut, simpan barang pribadi, dan periksa tangan serta kondisi tubuh. Bila merasa sakit saat bekerja, berhenti menangani makanan dan beri tahu pemimpin. Jangan menyembunyikan gejala atau hanya memakai sarung tangan untuk meneruskan tugas yang berisiko.

Kasus latihan: Sebelum menyiapkan salad, seorang pekerja merasa mual dan muntah sejak pagi, tetapi restoran sedang ramai.
Respons yang dianjurkan: Beri tahu pemimpin, jangan menyiapkan makanan, dan tunggu penetapan tugas sesuai prosedur restoran.`}: `Before your shift, change into your uniform, cover your hair, store personal belongings, and check your hands and general condition. If you feel ill while working, stop handling food and tell the supervisor. Do not hide symptoms or simply put on gloves to continue a risky task.

Practice scenario: Before preparing a salad, a worker feels nauseated and has been vomiting since morning, but the restaurant is busy.
Recommended response: Tell the supervisor, do not prepare food, and wait for a task assignment according to restaurant procedures.`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Ganti pakaian dan perlengkapan sesuai aturan restoran`}:                                                             `Change clothes and equipment according to restaurant rules`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Periksa kondisi tubuh dan tangan`}:                                                                                  `Check your general condition and hands`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Laporkan gejala atau luka kepada pemimpin`}:                                                                         `Report symptoms or injuries to the supervisor`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Mulai tugas setelah mendapat arahan`}:                                                                               `Start work after receiving instructions`,
	{field: "ssw.caution", source: `Jangan menangani makanan saat gejala sakit belum dilaporkan.`}:                                                   `Do not handle food before reporting illness symptoms.`,
	{field: "ssw.scenario", source: `Sebelum menyiapkan salad, seorang pekerja merasa mual dan muntah sejak pagi, tetapi restoran sedang ramai.`}:    `Before preparing a salad, a worker feels nauseated and has been vomiting since morning, but the restaurant is busy.`,
	{field: "ssw.response", source: `Beri tahu pemimpin, jangan menyiapkan makanan, dan tunggu penetapan tugas sesuai prosedur restoran.`}:           `Tell the supervisor, do not prepare food, and wait for a task assignment according to restaurant procedures.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `kondisi tubuh`}:                                                                                                  `physical condition`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `seragam`}:                                                                                                        `uniform`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Saya merasa tidak enak badan. Saya akan melapor kepada penanggung jawab.`}:                                       `I do not feel well. I will report to the person in charge.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Sebelum menangani makanan, periksa tangan dan pakaian.`}:                                                         `Before handling food, check your hands and clothing.`,
	{field: "ssw.title", source: `Cuci tangan dan pisahkan bahan mentah`}:                                                                            `Wash Hands and Separate Raw Ingredients`,
	{field: "ssw.objective", source: `Mencuci tangan pada saat yang tepat dan mencegah alat atau tangan memindahkan cemaran ke makanan siap makan.`}: `Wash your hands at the right times and prevent tools or hands from transferring contamination to ready-to-eat food.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Tangan, pisau, talenan, dan meja dapat memindahkan cemaran dari bahan mentah ke makanan yang tidak dimasak lagi. Cuci tangan setelah menyentuh daging mentah, sampah, toilet, uang, telepon, atau tugas pembersihan. Sarung tangan yang sama juga dapat memindahkan cemaran; ikuti aturan pergantian dan pemisahan alat restoran.`}: `Hands, knives, cutting boards, and counters can transfer contamination from raw ingredients to food that will not be cooked again. Wash your hands after touching raw meat, waste, toilets, money, phones, or cleaning tasks. The same gloves can also spread contamination; follow the restaurant's rules for changing gloves and separating equipment.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Simpan bahan dan talenan sesuai label atau warna yang ditetapkan restoran. Setelah menyiapkan daging mentah, hentikan tugas, cuci tangan, ganti sarung tangan jika digunakan, dan gunakan permukaan yang telah dibersihkan untuk makanan siap makan. Jika alat bersih terkena cairan mentah, pisahkan dan minta pencucian ulang.

Kasus latihan: Setelah memotong ayam mentah, pekerja mengambil irisan tomat dengan sarung tangan yang sama untuk salad.
Respons yang dianjurkan: Hentikan penyajian salad, pisahkan alat dan bahan yang mungkin terkena, cuci tangan, lalu beri tahu pemimpin untuk penanganan ulang.`}: `Store ingredients and cutting boards according to the restaurant's labels or color coding. After preparing raw meat, stop, wash your hands, change gloves if worn, and use a cleaned surface for ready-to-eat food. If a clean tool is exposed to raw juices, set it aside and request rewashing.

Practice scenario: After cutting raw chicken, a worker uses the same gloves to pick up tomato slices for a salad.
Recommended response: Stop serving the salad, separate tools and ingredients that may be affected, wash your hands, and tell the supervisor so they can be handled again.`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Kenali label atau kode alat untuk tiap jenis bahan`}:                                                                                       `Know the label or equipment code for each ingredient type`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Pisahkan bahan mentah dari makanan siap makan`}:                                                                                            `Separate raw ingredients from ready-to-eat food`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Cuci tangan setelah kontak dengan bahan mentah atau tugas kotor`}:                                                                          `Wash your hands after handling raw ingredients or doing dirty tasks`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Bersihkan atau ganti alat sebelum berpindah tugas`}:                                                                                        `Clean or replace tools before switching tasks`,
	{field: "ssw.caution", source: `Jangan memakai pisau atau sarung tangan yang sama untuk bahan mentah dan makanan siap makan.`}:                                          `Do not use the same knife or gloves for raw ingredients and ready-to-eat food.`,
	{field: "ssw.scenario", source: `Setelah memotong ayam mentah, pekerja mengambil irisan tomat dengan sarung tangan yang sama untuk salad.`}:                             `After cutting raw chicken, a worker uses the same gloves to pick up tomato slices for a salad.`,
	{field: "ssw.response", source: `Hentikan penyajian salad, pisahkan alat dan bahan yang mungkin terkena, cuci tangan, lalu beri tahu pemimpin untuk penanganan ulang.`}: `Stop serving the salad, separate tools and ingredients that may be affected, wash your hands, and tell the supervisor so they can be handled again.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `daging mentah`}:                                                                                                                         `raw meat`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `talenan`}:                                                                                                                               `cutting board`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `kontaminasi silang`}:                                                                                                                    `cross-contamination`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Talenan ini untuk daging mentah.`}:                                                                                                      `This cutting board is for raw meat.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Saya ganti dengan alat untuk salad.`}:                                                                                                   `I will replace it with tools for the salad.`,
	{field: "ssw.title", source: `Waktu, suhu, dan penyimpanan bahan`}:                                                                                                      `Time, Temperature, and Ingredient Storage`,
	{field: "ssw.objective", source: `Memeriksa kondisi simpan serta mencatat waktu atau suhu sesuai batas pada label dan prosedur restoran.`}:                              `Check storage conditions and record time or temperature according to label limits and restaurant procedures.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Bahan dingin, panas, dan makanan siap saji memiliki syarat penyimpanan sesuai produk dan rencana restoran. Pekerja menggunakan termometer dan batas yang ditulis untuk bahan tersebut, bukan mengandalkan sentuhan atau angka hafalan. Penutup wadah, label waktu, dan pemisahan bahan membantu menjaga keamanan dan mutu selama giliran.`}: `Cold, hot, and ready-to-eat foods have storage requirements based on the product and restaurant plan. Use a thermometer and the limits written for that ingredient rather than relying on touch or memorized numbers. Container lids, time labels, and ingredient separation help maintain safety and quality during a shift.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Periksa suhu dengan alat yang ditetapkan, bersihkan probe sesuai prosedur, lalu catat waktu dan hasil. Simpan wadah tertutup dengan identitas yang terbaca. Bila suhu atau waktu melewati batas restoran, label hilang, atau alat tidak berfungsi, tahan bahan dan minta pemimpin menentukan langkah berikutnya.

Kasus latihan: Sup yang akan disajikan tidak memiliki label waktu, dan termometer stasiun sedang menunjukkan pesan kesalahan.
Respons yang dianjurkan: Jangan sajikan sup. Tahan wadah, laporkan label dan alat yang bermasalah, lalu tunggu pemeriksaan sesuai prosedur.`}: `Check the temperature with the designated instrument, clean the probe according to procedure, and record the time and result. Keep containers covered with readable identification. If the temperature or time exceeds restaurant limits, a label is missing, or equipment does not work, hold the ingredient and ask the supervisor to decide what to do next.

Practice scenario: Soup ready to be served has no time label, and the station thermometer is displaying an error.
Recommended response: Do not serve the soup. Hold the container, report the missing label and faulty instrument, and wait for an inspection according to procedure.`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Baca label waktu dan syarat penyimpanan`}:                                                                                         `Read time labels and storage requirements`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Gunakan alat ukur sesuai instruksi`}:                                                                                              `Use measuring equipment as instructed`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Catat waktu dan suhu aktual`}:                                                                                                     `Record the actual time and temperature`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Tahan bahan yang menyimpang dan laporkan`}:                                                                                        `Hold and report ingredients that are outside the limits`,
	{field: "ssw.caution", source: `Jangan menilai keamanan makanan hanya dengan mencium, menyentuh, atau melihatnya.`}:                                            `Do not judge food safety by smell, touch, or appearance alone.`,
	{field: "ssw.scenario", source: `Sup yang akan disajikan tidak memiliki label waktu, dan termometer stasiun sedang menunjukkan pesan kesalahan.`}:              `Soup ready to be served has no time label, and the station thermometer is displaying an error.`,
	{field: "ssw.response", source: `Jangan sajikan sup. Tahan wadah, laporkan label dan alat yang bermasalah, lalu tunggu pemeriksaan sesuai prosedur.`}:          `Do not serve the soup. Hold the container, report the missing label and faulty instrument, and wait for an inspection according to procedure.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `termometer`}:                                                                                                                   `thermometer`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Termometer menampilkan pesan kesalahan.`}:                                                                                      `The thermometer is displaying an error.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Saya menahan sup ini dan meminta pemeriksaan penanggung jawab.`}:                                                               `I am holding this soup and requesting an inspection by the person in charge.`,
	{field: "ssw.description", source: `Menyiapkan stasiun kerja, menangani permintaan khusus dengan konfirmasi yang jujur, dan mencegah kontak silang di dapur.`}: `Prepare workstations, handle special requests with clear confirmation, and prevent cross-contact in the kitchen.`,
	{field: "ssw.title", source: `Persiapan bahan dan stasiun kerja`}:                                                                                              `Ingredient and Workstation Preparation`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `selamat datang`}:                                                                                                               `welcome`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `tempat duduk`}:                                                                                                                 `seat`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `mengantar atau memberi petunjuk`}:                                                                                              `to escort or give directions`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Selamat datang. Untuk berapa orang?`}:                                                                                          `Welcome. How many people are in your party?`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Saya antar ke tempat duduk ini.`}:                                                                                              `I will show you to this table.`,
	{field: "ssw.title", source: `Mencatat pesanan dan mengulang konfirmasi`}:                                                                                      `Recording Orders and Repeating Them for Confirmation`,
	{field: "ssw.objective", source: `Mendengarkan pesanan, mencatat jumlah serta pilihan dengan benar, dan mengulang poin penting kepada tamu.`}:                  `Listen to orders, accurately record quantities and choices, and repeat key details to guests.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Pesanan mencakup hidangan, jumlah, pilihan ukuran, tingkat kematangan bila berlaku, dan permintaan khusus. Mengulang pesanan membantu menemukan salah dengar sebelum tiket dikirim. Bila kata atau pilihan tidak dipahami, pekerja bertanya dengan sopan dan menggunakan gambar menu atau nomor hidangan sebagai bantuan.`}: `An order includes the dish, quantity, size, cooking level when applicable, and special requests. Repeating the order helps catch misunderstandings before sending the ticket. If a word or choice is unclear, ask politely and use the menu picture or dish number to help.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Catat pesanan segera pada sistem atau tiket untuk meja yang benar. Ulangi item dan jumlah, tanyakan kembali pilihan yang belum jelas, lalu kirim tiket ke dapur. Jangan memasukkan catatan alergi sebagai pilihan biasa; sampaikan kepada pemimpin dan ikuti alur khusus restoran.

Kasus latihan: Pelanggan memesan dua hidangan dan menyebut satu tanpa bawang, tetapi pekerja hanya mencatat nama hidangannya.
Respons yang dianjurkan: Konfirmasi kembali permintaan tanpa bawang, perbarui tiket meja yang benar, lalu pastikan dapur menerima catatan itu.`}: `Record orders promptly in the system or on a ticket for the correct table. Repeat the items and quantities, ask again about unclear choices, then send the ticket to the kitchen. Do not enter allergy notes as ordinary preferences; tell the supervisor and follow the restaurant's special procedure.

Practice scenario: A customer orders two dishes and requests one without onions, but the worker records only the dish names.
Recommended response: Confirm the no-onion request, update the ticket for the correct table, and make sure the kitchen receives the note.`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Dengarkan pesanan sampai selesai`}:                                                                                          `Listen to the full order`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Catat item dan jumlah pada meja yang benar`}:                                                                                `Record the items and quantities for the correct table`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Ulangi pilihan utama untuk konfirmasi`}:                                                                                     `Repeat the key choices for confirmation`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Kirim tiket dan sampaikan permintaan khusus`}:                                                                               `Send the ticket and communicate special requests`,
	{field: "ssw.caution", source: `Jangan mengirim tiket ketika jumlah atau pilihan pelanggan masih belum jelas.`}:                                          `Do not send the ticket while the customer's quantity or choices are still unclear.`,
	{field: "ssw.scenario", source: `Pelanggan memesan dua hidangan dan menyebut satu tanpa bawang, tetapi pekerja hanya mencatat nama hidangannya.`}:        `A customer orders two dishes and requests one without onions, but the worker records only the dish names.`,
	{field: "ssw.response", source: `Konfirmasi kembali permintaan tanpa bawang, perbarui tiket meja yang benar, lalu pastikan dapur menerima catatan itu.`}: `Confirm the no-onion request, update the ticket for the correct table, and make sure the kitchen receives the note.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `jumlah unit`}:                                                                                                            `quantity`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Pesanannya dua kari, benar?`}:                                                                                            `Two curries, is that correct?`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Tanpa bawang bombai, betul?`}:                                                                                            `No onion, correct?`,
	{field: "ssw.title", source: `Mengantar hidangan dan memeriksa meja`}:                                                                                    `Serving Dishes and Checking the Table`,
	{field: "ssw.objective", source: `Mencocokkan hidangan dengan tiket dan meja serta membawa nampan dengan aman.`}:                                         `Match dishes to tickets and tables, and carry trays safely.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Piring yang benar harus sampai ke meja dan pelanggan yang memesan. Sebelum berangkat, pekerja membaca nama atau nomor hidangan pada tiket, memeriksa jumlah dan modifikasi, serta memastikan piring dan nampan stabil. Jalur antarmeja dapat sempit; utamakan pandangan dan keseimbangan, bukan kecepatan.`}: `Each dish must reach the table and customer who ordered it. Before leaving, read the dish name or number on the ticket, check the quantity and modifications, and make sure the plates and tray are stable. Routes between tables can be narrow; prioritize visibility and balance over speed.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Angkat nampan dengan posisi stabil dan gunakan jalur yang tidak licin. Di meja, sebut nama hidangan secara singkat dan letakkan tanpa menyentuh permukaan makan. Jika satu item tidak cocok dengan tiket atau pelanggan mengatakan hidangan bukan pesanannya, jangan tinggalkan; tahan dan bawa kembali ke titik pemeriksaan.

Kasus latihan: Di lorong, pekerja mendapati tiket di nampan tertulis meja 8, tetapi rekan memanggilnya ke meja 6.
Respons yang dianjurkan: Berhenti di tempat aman dan cocokkan tiket dengan nomor meja; jangan menyerahkan hidangan sampai tujuan dipastikan.`}: `Lift the tray steadily and use a route that is not slippery. At the table, briefly name each dish and set it down without touching the eating surface. If an item does not match the ticket or the customer says it is not what they ordered, do not leave it; hold it and take it back to the check point.

Practice scenario: In the aisle, a worker sees a ticket on the tray for table 8, but a colleague calls them to table 6.
Recommended response: Stop in a safe place and match the ticket to the table number; do not hand over the dish until its destination is confirmed.`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Cocokkan hidangan dan jumlah dengan tiket`}:                                                                                                   `Match dishes and quantities to the ticket`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Periksa modifikasi serta kestabilan nampan`}:                                                                                                  `Check modifications and tray stability`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Bawa melalui jalur yang aman`}:                                                                                                                `Carry the dishes along a safe route`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Sebutkan hidangan dan pastikan meja yang benar`}:                                                                                              `Name the dishes and confirm the correct table`,
	{field: "ssw.caution", source: `Jangan menyerahkan piring yang identitas meja atau pesannya belum pasti.`}:                                                                 `Do not hand over a dish if its table or order identity is uncertain.`,
	{field: "ssw.scenario", source: `Di lorong, pekerja mendapati tiket di nampan tertulis meja 8, tetapi rekan memanggilnya ke meja 6.`}:                                      `In the aisle, a worker sees a ticket on the tray for table 8, but a colleague calls them to table 6.`,
	{field: "ssw.response", source: `Berhenti di tempat aman dan cocokkan tiket dengan nomor meja; jangan menyerahkan hidangan sampai tujuan dipastikan.`}:                     `Stop in a safe place and match the ticket to the table number; do not hand over the dish until its destination is confirmed.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `mengantar hidangan`}:                                                                                                                       `serving dishes`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `hidangan`}:                                                                                                                                 `dish`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `piring`}:                                                                                                                                   `plate`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Ini ikan panggang Anda.`}:                                                                                                                  `Here is your grilled fish.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Saya akan memastikan nomor meja.`}:                                                                                                         `I will confirm the table number.`,
	{field: "ssw.description", source: `Menangani keluhan dengan tenang, menjaga ketepatan transaksi, serta membersihkan dan menyerahkan status restoran pada akhir giliran.`}: `Handle complaints calmly, process transactions accurately, and clean and hand over restaurant status at the end of a shift.`,
	{field: "ssw.title", source: `Menangani keluhan pelanggan`}:                                                                                                                `Handling Customer Complaints`,
	{field: "ssw.objective", source: `Mendengarkan keluhan, mengulangi masalah dengan sopan, dan meminta bantuan pemimpin untuk keputusan atau risiko keselamatan.`}:           `Listen to complaints, politely repeat the issue, and ask the supervisor for help with decisions or safety risks.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Keluhan dapat berkaitan dengan hidangan salah, keterlambatan, mutu, alergi, atau keselamatan. Pekerja tetap tenang, mendengarkan tanpa berdebat, meminta maaf atas ketidaknyamanan, dan mengumpulkan fakta. Penggantian, pengembalian uang, atau penanganan insiden mengikuti wewenang restoran; masalah kesehatan segera diserahkan kepada pemimpin.`}: `Complaints may concern an incorrect dish, delays, quality, allergies, or safety. Stay calm, listen without arguing, apologize for the inconvenience, and gather the facts. Replacements, refunds, and incident handling must follow the restaurant's authority rules; immediately refer health concerns to the supervisor.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Ucapkan bahwa Anda akan memeriksa, ulangi masalah agar pelanggan merasa didengar, lalu hubungi pemimpin. Jangan menyalahkan dapur atau menjanjikan kompensasi yang tidak Anda berwenang berikan. Jika pelanggan merasa sakit atau ada kemungkinan bahaya makanan, hentikan penjualan hidangan terkait dan laporkan segera.

Kasus latihan: Pelanggan mengatakan setelah mencicipi hidangan, ia merasa tidak sehat dan ingin tahu siapa yang bertanggung jawab.
Respons yang dianjurkan: Tanggapi dengan tenang, hentikan penyajian hidangan terkait, panggil pemimpin, dan catat waktu serta hidangan tanpa berspekulasi.`}: `Say that you will check, repeat the issue so the customer knows they were heard, then contact the supervisor. Do not blame the kitchen or promise compensation beyond your authority. If the customer feels ill or food may be unsafe, stop selling the related dish and report it immediately.

Practice scenario: After tasting a dish, a customer says they feel unwell and asks who is responsible.
Recommended response: Respond calmly, stop serving the dish, call the supervisor, and record the time and dish without speculation.`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Dengarkan pelanggan tanpa menyela`}:                                                                                                     `Listen to the customer without interrupting`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Ulangi inti masalah dan minta maaf dengan sopan`}:                                                                                       `Repeat the main issue and apologize politely`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Hubungi pemimpin untuk keputusan sesuai wewenang`}:                                                                                      `Contact the supervisor for a decision within their authority`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Catat fakta dan tindak lanjut yang diperlukan`}:                                                                                         `Record the facts and required follow-up`,
	{field: "ssw.caution", source: `Jangan berdebat, menyalahkan pelanggan, atau menjanjikan tindakan di luar wewenang.`}:                                                `Do not argue, blame the customer, or promise actions beyond your authority.`,
	{field: "ssw.scenario", source: `Pelanggan mengatakan setelah mencicipi hidangan, ia merasa tidak sehat dan ingin tahu siapa yang bertanggung jawab.`}:               `After tasting a dish, a customer says they feel unwell and asks who is responsible.`,
	{field: "ssw.response", source: `Tanggapi dengan tenang, hentikan penyajian hidangan terkait, panggil pemimpin, dan catat waktu serta hidangan tanpa berspekulasi.`}: `Respond calmly, stop serving the dish, call the supervisor, and record the time and dish without speculation.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `keadaan`}:                                                                                                                            `condition`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Mohon maaf. Saya akan segera memeriksanya.`}:                                                                                         `I am sorry. I will check that right away.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Saya akan memanggil penanggung jawab.`}:                                                                                              `I will call the person in charge.`,
	{field: "ssw.objective", source: `Menyiapkan bahan, alat, porsi, dan urutan kerja berdasarkan resep serta tiket pesanan yang benar.`}:                                `Prepare ingredients, tools, portions, and work sequence according to the correct recipe and order ticket.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Persiapan yang rapi mengurangi salah bahan, menunggu, dan gerak berulang saat layanan sibuk. Pekerja memeriksa resep, porsi, alat, dan kondisi bahan sebelum menyiapkan stasiun. Makanan siap makan dipisahkan dari bahan mentah; pisau, panas, dan alat listrik digunakan hanya sesuai pelatihan.`}: `Organized preparation reduces ingredient mix-ups, waiting, and repeated movements during busy service. Check the recipe, portions, tools, and ingredient condition before setting up a station. Keep ready-to-eat food separate from raw ingredients; use knives, heat, and electrical equipment only within your training.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Susun bahan dalam wadah berlabel, ambil secukupnya untuk giliran, dan simpan sisanya sesuai syaratnya. Baca tiket dengan teliti; bila ada catatan yang tidak terbaca, konfirmasi sebelum memasak. Bersihkan tumpahan segera dengan cara yang tidak mencemari bahan atau membuat lantai licin.

Kasus latihan: Tiket memesan sup sayur, tetapi wadah di stasiun tidak berlabel dan isinya tidak dapat dikenali.
Respons yang dianjurkan: Jangan gunakan isi wadah. Pisahkan dan minta identifikasi dari pemimpin sebelum menyiapkan pesanan.`}: `Arrange ingredients in labeled containers, take only what is needed for the shift, and store the rest as required. Read tickets carefully; if a note is unreadable, confirm it before cooking. Clean spills promptly without contaminating ingredients or making the floor slippery.

Practice scenario: The ticket is for vegetable soup, but an unlabelled container at the station has unidentified contents.
Recommended response: Do not use the contents. Set the container aside and ask the supervisor to identify them before preparing the order.`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Baca resep dan kebutuhan pesanan`}:                                                                                                         `Read the recipe and order requirements`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Periksa bahan, label, dan alat yang diperlukan`}:                                                                                           `Check the required ingredients, labels, and tools`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Siapkan bahan dalam wadah terpisah dan beridentitas`}:                                                                                      `Prepare ingredients in separate, labeled containers`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Rapikan stasiun dan konfirmasi hal yang tidak jelas`}:                                                                                      `Organize the station and confirm anything unclear`,
	{field: "ssw.caution", source: `Jangan menebak bahan atau porsi ketika tiket dan label tidak cocok.`}:                                                                   `Do not guess the ingredient or portion when the ticket and label do not match.`,
	{field: "ssw.scenario", source: `Tiket memesan sup sayur, tetapi wadah di stasiun tidak berlabel dan isinya tidak dapat dikenali.`}:                                     `The ticket is for vegetable soup, but an unlabelled container at the station has unidentified contents.`,
	{field: "ssw.response", source: `Jangan gunakan isi wadah. Pisahkan dan minta identifikasi dari pemimpin sebelum menyiapkan pesanan.`}:                                  `Do not use the contents. Set the container aside and ask the supervisor to identify them before preparing the order.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `persiapan bahan`}:                                                                                                                       `ingredient preparation`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `tiket pesanan`}:                                                                                                                         `order ticket`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `takaran`}:                                                                                                                               `measurement`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Mohon konfirmasi nama bahan ini.`}:                                                                                                      `Please confirm the name of this ingredient.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Saya akan menyiapkan setelah membaca tiket pesanan.`}:                                                                                   `I will prepare it after reading the order ticket.`,
	{field: "ssw.title", source: `Menerima pertanyaan alergi pelanggan`}:                                                                                                    `Responding to Customer Allergy Questions`,
	{field: "ssw.objective", source: `Mendengarkan permintaan alergi, memeriksa informasi menu, dan menghubungi dapur atau pemimpin tanpa membuat janji yang tidak pasti.`}: `Listen to allergy requests, check menu information, and contact the kitchen or supervisor without making unverified promises.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Alergi makanan dapat menimbulkan reaksi serius. Informasi bahan dan risiko kontak silang dapat berbeda menurut menu, pemasok, serta cara memasak. Pelayan memakai panduan alergi restoran yang terbaru dan bertanya kepada pihak berwenang bila jawaban tidak jelas; jangan menebak dari nama hidangan atau menjamin bahwa hidangan bebas alergen tanpa dasar.`}: `Food allergies can cause serious reactions. Ingredient information and cross-contact risks can vary by menu, supplier, and cooking method. Use the restaurant's current allergy guide and ask an authorized person when an answer is unclear. Do not guess from a dish's name or claim it is allergen-free without confirmation.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Dengarkan nama bahan yang dihindari, ulangi untuk memastikan, lalu periksa panduan atau sistem menu. Sampaikan jawaban yang diketahui dengan jelas; bila informasi tidak cukup, beri tahu pelanggan bahwa Anda akan memastikan dan segera hubungi pemimpin atau dapur. Jangan mengubah resep atau menyuruh dapur mengabaikan prosedur.

Kasus latihan: Pelanggan bertanya apakah saus mengandung kacang, tetapi daftar bahan di stasiun belum diperbarui.
Respons yang dianjurkan: Jangan menebak. Katakan akan memeriksa, tahan rekomendasi hidangan, dan minta pemimpin memverifikasi informasi terbaru.`}: `Listen to the ingredient the customer needs to avoid, repeat it to confirm, then check the guide or menu system. Clearly share what is known. If the information is insufficient, tell the customer you will confirm it and contact the supervisor or kitchen right away. Do not change the recipe or ask the kitchen to ignore procedures.

Practice scenario: A customer asks whether a sauce contains peanuts, but the ingredient list at the station has not been updated.
Recommended response: Do not guess. Say you will check, hold off on recommending the dish, and ask the supervisor to verify the latest information.`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Dengarkan permintaan dan catat bahan yang dihindari`}:                                                                         `Listen to the request and note the ingredient to avoid`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Ulangi permintaan untuk memastikan maksud pelanggan`}:                                                                         `Repeat the request to confirm what the customer means`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Periksa panduan dan konfirmasi dengan pihak berwenang`}:                                                                       `Check the guide and confirm with an authorized person`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Sampaikan informasi yang terverifikasi atau pilihan aman`}:                                                                    `Share verified information or a safe alternative`,
	{field: "ssw.caution", source: `Jangan menjawab “aman” berdasarkan perkiraan atau hanya karena bahan tidak terlihat di piring.`}:                           `Do not say a dish is “safe” based on a guess or simply because the ingredient is not visible on the plate.`,
	{field: "ssw.scenario", source: `Pelanggan bertanya apakah saus mengandung kacang, tetapi daftar bahan di stasiun belum diperbarui.`}:                      `A customer asks whether a sauce contains peanuts, but the ingredient list at the station has not been updated.`,
	{field: "ssw.response", source: `Jangan menebak. Katakan akan memeriksa, tahan rekomendasi hidangan, dan minta pemimpin memverifikasi informasi terbaru.`}: `Do not guess. Say you will check, hold off on recommending the dish, and ask the supervisor to verify the latest information.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `bahan`}:                                          `ingredient`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `saya akan memeriksa`}:                            `I will check`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Apakah saus ini mengandung kacang?`}:             `Does this sauce contain peanuts?`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Saya akan memeriksanya, mohon tunggu sebentar.`}: `I will check that for you. Please wait a moment.`,
	{field: "ssw.title", source: `Perubahan pesanan dan pencegahan kontak silang`}:   `Order Changes and Cross-Contact Prevention`,
	{field: "ssw.objective", source: `Meneruskan perubahan pesanan ke dapur dengan jelas dan memastikan alat serta alur kerja sesuai permintaan terverifikasi.`}:                                                                                                                                                                                                                           `Clearly pass order changes to the kitchen and make sure tools and workflow follow the verified request.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Catatan seperti tanpa telur atau pisahkan saus mengubah cara dapur menyiapkan dan menyajikan hidangan. Tiket harus memuat perubahan dengan jelas dan terhubung ke meja atau nomor pesanan yang benar. Jika permintaan berkaitan dengan alergi, dapur memakai prosedur kontak silang yang sudah ditetapkan; perubahan kecil tidak boleh dianggap sepele.`}: `Notes such as “no egg” or “sauce on the side” change how the kitchen prepares and serves a dish. The ticket must state the change clearly and be linked to the correct table or order number. For allergy-related requests, the kitchen follows established cross-contact procedures; do not treat small changes as unimportant.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Ulangi perubahan kepada pelanggan, masukkan pada sistem atau tiket, lalu pastikan dapur menerima versi yang benar. Bila tiket tertukar atau modifikasi belum dikonfirmasi, tahan hidangan sebelum dibawa. Gunakan piring dan alat yang ditentukan untuk pesanan tersebut; jangan sekadar mengikis bahan dari hidangan jadi.

Kasus latihan: Pelanggan meminta hidangan tanpa telur karena alergi; tiket lama sudah masuk dapur tanpa catatan itu.
Respons yang dianjurkan: Jangan bawa hidangan lama. Hentikan penyajian, beri tahu dapur dan pemimpin, lalu buat tiket yang benar dan ikuti prosedur alergi.`}: `Repeat the change to the customer, enter it in the system or ticket, and make sure the kitchen receives the correct version. If tickets are mixed up or a modification is unconfirmed, hold the dish before it is carried out. Use the plate and tools designated for the order; do not simply scrape an ingredient off a finished dish.

Practice scenario: A customer requests an egg-free dish because of an allergy, but the original ticket has already gone to the kitchen without that note.
Recommended response: Do not bring out the original dish. Stop service, tell the kitchen and supervisor, then create the correct ticket and follow allergy procedures.`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Ulangi perubahan pesanan kepada pelanggan`}:                                                                                              `Repeat the order change to the customer`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Masukkan catatan pada tiket yang benar`}:                                                                                                 `Enter the note on the correct ticket`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Konfirmasi penerimaan perubahan oleh dapur`}:                                                                                             `Confirm that the kitchen received the change`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Periksa hidangan dan alat sebelum disajikan`}:                                                                                            `Check the dish and tools before serving`,
	{field: "ssw.caution", source: `Jangan menghapus bahan dari hidangan yang sudah jadi untuk memenuhi permintaan alergi.`}:                                              `Do not remove an ingredient from a finished dish to meet an allergy request.`,
	{field: "ssw.scenario", source: `Pelanggan meminta hidangan tanpa telur karena alergi; tiket lama sudah masuk dapur tanpa catatan itu.`}:                              `A customer requests an egg-free dish because of an allergy, but the original ticket has already gone to the kitchen without that note.`,
	{field: "ssw.response", source: `Jangan bawa hidangan lama. Hentikan penyajian, beri tahu dapur dan pemimpin, lalu buat tiket yang benar dan ikuti prosedur alergi.`}: `Do not bring out the original dish. Stop service, tell the kitchen and supervisor, then create the correct ticket and follow allergy procedures.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `terpisah`}:                                                                                                                            `separate`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Saya akan mengubah pesanan menjadi tanpa telur.`}:                                                                                     `I will change the order to egg-free.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Mohon periksa tiket yang baru.`}:                                                                                                      `Please check the new ticket.`,
	{field: "ssw.description", source: `Menggunakan bahasa sopan dan konfirmasi sederhana saat menyambut, mencatat pesanan, serta mengantarkan hidangan.`}:                `Use polite language and simple confirmations when welcoming guests, recording orders, and serving dishes.`,
	{field: "ssw.title", source: `Menyambut tamu dan mengantar ke meja`}:                                                                                                  `Welcoming Guests and Showing Them to Their Table`,
	{field: "ssw.objective", source: `Menyapa tamu, memastikan jumlah orang atau reservasi, dan mengantar ke meja yang sesuai.`}:                                          `Greet guests, confirm the party size or reservation, and show them to the appropriate table.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Sambutan awal membantu tamu merasa diterima dan mengatur alur meja. Pekerja memakai salam sopan, menanyakan jumlah orang bila diperlukan, dan memastikan reservasi tanpa menyebut informasi pribadi dengan suara keras. Jalur pelayanan harus bebas dari kereta, barang, dan tumpahan agar tamu maupun staf dapat lewat dengan aman.`}: `A warm greeting helps guests feel welcome and supports table flow. Greet guests politely, ask the party size when needed, and confirm reservations without saying personal information aloud. Keep service routes clear of carts, belongings, and spills so guests and staff can pass safely.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Sapa tamu, dengarkan jawaban, lalu ulangi informasi penting seperti nama reservasi atau jumlah orang. Bila meja belum siap, jelaskan perkiraan hanya setelah memeriksa keadaan dan minta mereka menunggu di tempat yang ditentukan. Jangan menjanjikan meja tertentu tanpa konfirmasi sistem.

Kasus latihan: Tamu datang tanpa reservasi, dan meja yang baru dikosongkan belum dibersihkan.
Respons yang dianjurkan: Sapa tamu, jelaskan bahwa meja sedang disiapkan, dan minta mereka menunggu di area yang ditentukan sampai meja dikonfirmasi siap.`}: `Greet guests, listen to their answers, and repeat important information such as the reservation name or party size. If a table is not ready, give an estimated wait only after checking and ask guests to wait in the designated area. Do not promise a particular table without confirming it in the system.

Practice scenario: Guests arrive without a reservation, and a recently vacated table has not yet been cleaned.
Recommended response: Greet them, explain that the table is being prepared, and ask them to wait in the designated area until the table is confirmed ready.`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Sapa tamu dengan ungkapan yang sopan`}:                                                                                                  `Greet guests politely`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Tanyakan reservasi atau jumlah orang bila perlu`}:                                                                                       `Ask about a reservation or party size when needed`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Periksa meja dan jalur berjalan`}:                                                                                                       `Check the table and walking route`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Antar tamu dan sampaikan menu`}:                                                                                                         `Show guests to their table and provide the menu`,
	{field: "ssw.caution", source: `Jangan menyebut data reservasi pribadi dengan suara keras di depan orang lain.`}:                                                     `Do not say private reservation details aloud in front of others.`,
	{field: "ssw.scenario", source: `Tamu datang tanpa reservasi, dan meja yang baru dikosongkan belum dibersihkan.`}:                                                    `Guests arrive without a reservation, and a recently vacated table has not yet been cleaned.`,
	{field: "ssw.response", source: `Sapa tamu, jelaskan bahwa meja sedang disiapkan, dan minta mereka menunggu di area yang ditentukan sampai meja dikonfirmasi siap.`}: `Greet them, explain that the table is being prepared, and ask them to wait in the designated area until the table is confirmed ready.`,
	{field: "ssw.title", source: `Pembayaran dan pemeriksaan tagihan`}:                                                                                                   `Payment and Bill Checks`,
	{field: "ssw.objective", source: `Mencocokkan tagihan dengan pesanan, menerima pembayaran sesuai prosedur, dan menjaga informasi pelanggan.`}:                        `Match bills to orders, accept payments according to procedure, and protect customer information.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Pembayaran yang tepat bergantung pada tagihan meja, jumlah, metode pembayaran, dan aturan kasir. Pekerja memeriksa total pada sistem dan menjelaskan biaya dengan jelas bila pelanggan bertanya. Uang tunai, kartu, dan aplikasi pembayaran ditangani sesuai petunjuk; jangan menyimpan kata sandi, nomor kartu, atau data pribadi pelanggan di luar sistem resmi.`}: `Accurate payment depends on the table bill, amount, payment method, and cashier procedures. Check the total in the system and explain charges clearly if customers ask. Handle cash, cards, and payment apps as instructed; do not store passwords, card numbers, or customer information outside the official system.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Sebelum menutup transaksi, cocokkan nomor meja dan item pada tagihan. Sebut jumlah yang harus dibayar, proses metode yang dipilih pelanggan, lalu berikan bukti pembayaran bila sistem memintanya. Jika pembayaran ditolak atau jumlah berbeda, jangan mengulang transaksi tanpa memastikan status pertama; panggil pemimpin atau ikuti alur kasir.

Kasus latihan: Terminal pembayaran menampilkan pesan menunggu setelah kartu pelanggan disentuhkan, dan pelanggan meminta pekerja mencoba lagi.
Respons yang dianjurkan: Periksa status transaksi pada sistem atau minta bantuan pemimpin sebelum mengulang, agar pelanggan tidak tertagih dua kali.`}: `Before closing a transaction, match the table number and items on the bill. State the amount due, process the customer's chosen payment method, and provide a receipt if the system requires it. If a payment is declined or the amount differs, do not retry until the first transaction's status is confirmed; call the supervisor or follow cashier procedures.

Practice scenario: The payment terminal shows a pending message after the customer taps their card, and the customer asks the worker to try again.
Recommended response: Check the transaction status in the system or ask the supervisor before retrying, so the customer is not charged twice.`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Cocokkan meja dan item pada tagihan`}:                                                                                                 `Match the table and items on the bill`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Sampaikan jumlah pembayaran dengan jelas`}:                                                                                            `Clearly state the amount due`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Proses metode pembayaran sesuai sistem`}:                                                                                              `Process the payment method through the system`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Konfirmasi hasil transaksi dan serahkan bukti`}:                                                                                       `Confirm the transaction result and provide a receipt`,
	{field: "ssw.caution", source: `Jangan mencatat atau menyimpan data pembayaran pelanggan di tempat pribadi.`}:                                                      `Do not write down or store customer payment details in a personal location.`,
	{field: "ssw.scenario", source: `Terminal pembayaran menampilkan pesan menunggu setelah kartu pelanggan disentuhkan, dan pelanggan meminta pekerja mencoba lagi.`}: `The payment terminal shows a pending message after the customer taps their card, and the customer asks the worker to try again.`,
	{field: "ssw.response", source: `Periksa status transaksi pada sistem atau minta bantuan pemimpin sebelum mengulang, agar pelanggan tidak tertagih dua kali.`}:     `Check the transaction status in the system or ask the supervisor before retrying, so the customer is not charged twice.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `pembayaran atau kasir`}:                                                                                                            `payment or cashier`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `tagihan`}:                                                                                                                          `bill`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `pembayaran`}:                                                                                                                       `payment`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Total pembayaran tiga ribu yen.`}:                                                                                                  `The total is three thousand yen.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Saya akan memeriksa status transaksi.`}:                                                                                            `I will check the transaction status.`,
	{field: "ssw.title", source: `Pembersihan, pengisian ulang, dan serah terima`}:                                                                                     `Cleaning, Restocking, and Handover`,
	{field: "ssw.objective", source: `Membersihkan stasiun, memilah limbah, mengisi kebutuhan giliran berikutnya, dan melaporkan pekerjaan yang belum selesai.`}:       `Clean the station, sort waste, restock for the next shift, and report unfinished work.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Penutupan restoran mencakup pembersihan alat dan meja, penyimpanan bahan, pembuangan limbah, dan pemeriksaan tugas yang tersisa. Bahan disimpan menurut label serta kondisi yang berlaku; bahan kimia pembersih disimpan terpisah. Catatan pergantian giliran perlu menjelaskan stok rendah, alat rusak, bahan ditahan, atau tugas yang belum selesai.`}: `Closing a restaurant includes cleaning tools and tables, storing ingredients, disposing of waste, and checking remaining tasks. Store ingredients according to their labels and required conditions; keep cleaning chemicals separate. Shift handover notes should identify low stock, damaged equipment, held ingredients, and unfinished tasks.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Ikuti daftar penutupan dari area bersih ke area kotor dengan alat pembersih yang sesuai. Pastikan bahan dikemas, diberi identitas, dan ditempatkan di lokasi simpan yang benar. Sebelum pulang, sampaikan kekurangan stok atau masalah peralatan kepada penerima giliran; jangan menulis pekerjaan selesai bila belum dilakukan.

Kasus latihan: Pada akhir giliran, wadah bahan terbuka belum diberi label waktu dan pembersihan lemari pendingin belum dicatat.
Respons yang dianjurkan: Pisahkan wadah untuk penilaian sesuai aturan, catat pembersihan yang belum selesai, dan serahkan kedua hal itu kepada pemimpin.`}: `Follow the closing checklist from clean areas to dirty areas using the appropriate cleaning tools. Make sure ingredients are packed, labeled, and placed in the correct storage location. Before leaving, tell the next shift about low stock or equipment problems; do not mark work complete if it has not been done.

Practice scenario: At the end of a shift, an open ingredient container has no time label and refrigerator cleaning has not been recorded.
Recommended response: Set the container aside for assessment according to rules, record the unfinished cleaning, and hand both items over to the supervisor.`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Periksa daftar tugas penutupan`}:                                                                                                      `Check the closing-task list`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Bersihkan dan simpan alat sesuai aturan area`}:                                                                                        `Clean and store tools according to area rules`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Tandai bahan, stok, atau pekerjaan yang masih terbuka`}:                                                                               `Flag ingredients, stock, or work that remains outstanding`,
	{field: "ssw.step", source: `Serahkan informasi kepada pemimpin atau giliran berikutnya`}:                                                                          `Hand the information over to the supervisor or next shift`,
	{field: "ssw.caution", source: `Jangan mencampur bahan kimia pembersih dengan pangan atau menyembunyikan tugas yang belum selesai.`}:                               `Do not mix cleaning chemicals with food or hide unfinished tasks.`,
	{field: "ssw.scenario", source: `Pada akhir giliran, wadah bahan terbuka belum diberi label waktu dan pembersihan lemari pendingin belum dicatat.`}:                `At the end of a shift, an open ingredient container has no time label and refrigerator cleaning has not been recorded.`,
	{field: "ssw.response", source: `Pisahkan wadah untuk penilaian sesuai aturan, catat pembersihan yang belum selesai, dan serahkan kedua hal itu kepada pemimpin.`}: `Set the container aside for assessment according to rules, record the unfinished cleaning, and hand both items over to the supervisor.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `limbah`}:                                                                 `waste`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Catatan pembersihan lemari pendingin belum selesai.`}:                    `The refrigerator-cleaning record is unfinished.`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `Saya akan meneruskan pekerjaan yang tersisa kepada giliran berikutnya.`}: `I will hand the remaining work over to the next shift.`,
	{field: "ssw.title", source: `Higiene dan keamanan pangan`}:                                              `Food Hygiene and Safety`,
	{field: "ssw.title", source: `Penerimaan tamu dan pelayanan meja`}:                                       `Guest Reception and Table Service`,
	{field: "ssw.title", source: `Persiapan hidangan dan permintaan alergi`}:                                 `Dish Preparation and Allergy Requests`,
	{field: "ssw.title", source: `Tanggapan masalah, pembayaran, dan penutupan`}:                             `Handling Issues, Payment, and Closing`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `pesanan`}:                                                                `order`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `reservasi`}:                                                              `reservation`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `suhu`}:                                                                   `temperature`,
	{field: "ssw.meaning", source: `tiket`}:                                                                  `order ticket`,
}
